---
source: crates/zendriver-mcp/tests/schema_snapshots.rs
expression: "schema_for! (tools::cloudflare::Outcome)"
---
$schema: "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"
title: Outcome
description: "Terminal outcome of a turnstile bypass attempt.\n\n`Solved` and `ChallengeGone` mirror the lib's `ClearanceOutcome`\nvariants. `Timeout` mirrors the lib's `ClearanceOutcome::TimedOut` — a\ndeadline in a turnstile flow is a normal outcome, not an error —\nsurfacing it on the success channel so agents can branch on `outcome`\nwithout try/catch around a timeout."
oneOf:
  - description: "Turnstile produced a token — the value held by the first matching\n`selectors.token_inputs` entry, `cf-turnstile-response` by default.\nThe token is available in [`SolveOutput::token`]."
    type: string
    const: solved
  - description: "Every challenge marker seen earlier is gone without a token, and the\npage has settled: a navigation replaced it with a parsed document\n(how Cloudflare's full-page challenge ends, on the page it guards),\nor it stayed without markers for three seconds. `token` will be\n`None`.\n\nNot proof the gate was passed: a replacement page whose every marker\nis added by script after it is parsed lands here too, so verify the\npage before treating what you read next as post-challenge content."
    type: string
    const: challenge_gone
  - description: "`timeout_ms` elapsed without reaching either success state. `token`\nwill be `None`. Not a hard error — agents can retry or give up."
    type: string
    const: timeout
